ps5webkit: RAR5 headers whose extra fields are all skipped are fine

process_head_file_extra() started from ret = ARCHIVE_FATAL and only the
fields it parses set it, so a header whose only extra field is one it
skips failed with no error message. rar -rr writes such a header: the
recovery record, a service header "RR" with just EX_SUBDATA. Every RAR5
archive with a recovery record (password or not) stopped at it, after its
last file, as "damaged". ret now starts at ARCHIVE_OK.

--- a/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_rar5.c
+++ b/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_rar5.c
@@ -2248,7 +2248,9 @@
 {
 	uint64_t extra_field_size;
 	uint64_t extra_field_id = 0;
-	int ret = ARCHIVE_FATAL;
+	/* OK unless a field's parser fails: a header whose fields are all
+	 * skipped (a recovery record's EX_SUBDATA, say) is fine. */
+	int ret = ARCHIVE_OK;
 	uint64_t var_size;
 
 	while(extra_data_size > 0) {
